cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reuse this evaluation, please cite it as below."
title: "DeepEval on A_Data — real extraction output vs. published SciCat record"
abstract: >-
  Scores a metadata draft produced by the PhysicsLLM extraction pipeline
  against the published SciCat record for the same dataset, using DeepEval as
  the harness. Metrics are tiered: deterministic exact and normalised matches
  gate, while an LLM-judged GEval metric is reported and never permitted to
  decide. Demonstrates the distinction the tiering exists for — a timestamp
  differing only in precision is absorbed by normalisation, while a dataset
  name that silently drops a qualifier is reported as real content loss.
type: software
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - research data management
  - metadata quality
  - DeepEval
  - evaluation
  - PETRA III
authors:
  - name: "PhysicsLLM C.5, Deutsches Elektronen-Synchrotron DESY"
    website: "https://physics-llm.erumdatahub.de/"
